#
# Conformance case: transaction/protocol-level-adequate-mvcc-snapshot.
#
# A logic:ConcurrentComposition whose run declares BOTH a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol
# (logic:declaredProtocol) and a logic:IsolationLevel (logic:declaredIsolationLevel). The
# native evaluator cross-checks whether the declared protocol's GUARANTEED CEILING reaches the
# declared level — a static consistency check between two contract facts, independent of the
# witnessed schedule (Principle 12) — and records logic:protocolLevelAdequacy.
# logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl guarantees snapshot isolation, so declaring
# logic:SnapshotIsolation is ADEQUATE (true). Multiversion needs no lock/timestamp events —
# the engine realizes snapshot isolation by construction — so logic:protocolEnforced holds
# structurally.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/transaction/protocol-level-adequate-mvcc-snapshot/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .

# The compile-time reasoning contract selects the transaction-path Evolution facet.
ex:TransactionContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:evolution logic:TransactionPathEvolution .
